# React UI (Material 3)

- Build screens with MUI Material 3 components; extract hooks for reusable logic.
- Prefer controlled forms (`TextField`, `Select`, `Checkbox`, `FormControl`) with clear validation and labels.
- List/table screens: use MUI loading/empty/error patterns (`Skeleton`, `Alert`, `EmptyState`-style layout).
- Keep interactive elements keyboard-accessible; rely on MUI a11y defaults and fix gaps.
- Avoid deep prop drilling; lift state or use context only for a real shared subtree.
- Prefer MUI layout primitives (`Stack`, `Box`, `Grid2`, `Container`) over custom flex/grid CSS.

```tsx
// ✅ Prefer explicit states with MUI
if (isLoading) return <Skeleton variant="rounded" height={120} />;
if (error) return <Alert severity="error">{error.message}</Alert>;
if (!items.length) return <Alert severity="info">No items yet</Alert>;
return <ItemTable items={items} />;
```
